<title>UK: UK government sets councils' standard spending.</title>
<headline>UK government sets councils' standard spending.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government has set the appropriate level of total standard spending for local authorities in England in the 1997/8 financial year at 45.66 billion stg, Environment Secretary John Gummer said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He said the figure provided for a 2.5 percent increase in local authority spending year-on-year. -- London Newsroom +44 171 5427767</p>
</text>
